title: EMR Connect › Problems › Fix a system that needs attention
route: /emr
intro: The three-step 'Fix' pop-up for a system whose read-only sign-in has expired: say what happened, renew the sign-in, test it. Nothing is written to the system.
dir: TD
also: In the demo the Billing system is the only system that Needs attention. The test always passes. Navigator does the fix, so a paused Navigator waits and 'Ask before acting' asks first.
---
screen s1 "Connection health\nBilling system · 'Needs attention' (amber) · '2 sync failures'\n'The read-only sign-in expired 2 hours ago, so remittances are not arriving. First step: renew the sign-in with Fix.'\nThe 'Action required' line says 'Billing system needs attention.' with its own 'Fix' button"
click c1 "Click 'Fix' on the row, or 'Fix' in the Action required line"
goto gg "Continues in: EMR Connect › Sync › When an agent is paused or asks first"
overlay o1 "Fix billing system\nThree short steps. Nothing is written to the system.\nSteps: What happened, Renew access, Test"

group gS1 "Step 1 of 3: What happened"
  process a1 "The issue text in an amber box"
  process a2 "'This is usually an expired sign-in. The first step is to renew the read-only access. The agents then pull the missed remittances.'"
  click a3 "Click 'Next'"
endgroup

group gS2 "Step 2 of 3: Renew access"
  input b1 "'Who approves the new sign-in' (required)\nFilled in with the system's contact, for example 'Billing lead'"
  input b2 "Tick 'I confirm the agents may read claims and remittances. They cannot change them.'"
  click b3 "Click 'Renew and test'"
  decision q1 "Name filled in and box ticked?"
  toast t1 "'Name the person who approves and confirm read-only access.'\nClears when either is changed"
  ext x1 "The approver renews the read-only sign-in\nDemo: simulated"
endgroup

group gS3 "Step 3 of 3: Test"
  process k1 "Signing in with the new read-only access"
  process k2 "Reading the latest remittance"
  process k3 "Matching it to a claim"
  toast t2 "'The test passed. Access is read-only, and nothing is written back.'"
  click f1 "Click 'Finish and reconnect'\nDimmed until the last check passes"
endgroup

group gSave "What finishing does"
  store v1 "Billing system becomes Connected\nLast sync now, the issue text is cleared"
  store v4 "Files pulled this week goes up by 12, the remittances the log line names\nSync failures go back to 0"
  agent v2 "Navigator logs 'Renewed the read-only sign-in for billing system and pulled 12 remittances'"
  toast v3 "'Billing system is connected'\n'Remittances are arriving again.'\nNo toast when Navigator is set to 'Act on its own'"
endgroup

click cx "Click 'Cancel' or the X, press Escape, or click the dimmed area\nThere is no 'Back' in this pop-up"
endx e2 "Pop-up closes\nThe system still Needs attention"
end e1 "Row shows 'Last sync just now', 'Connected', '0 sync failures' and a 'Sync now' button\nThe 'Action required' line moves on to the next item, or goes"
goto g1 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Manage › Disconnect and reconnect"
goto g2 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Manage › Reconnect a system"

s1 --> c1 --> gg --> o1 --> a1 --> a2 --> a3
a3 --> b1 --> b2 --> b3 --> q1
q1 -->|No| t1
t1 --> b1
q1 -->|Yes| k1
b3 -.-> x1
k1 --> k2 --> k3 --> t2 --> f1
f1 --> v1 & v2 & v3 & v4
v1 --> e1
v3 --> e1
o1 -.-> cx
cx --> e2
s1 -.->|Another way out| g1
s1 -.->|If it is disconnected later| g2
